2026-11-06T02:58:46.4170796Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T02:58:46.4179627Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T02:58:46.4179936Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T02:58:46.4180186Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T02:58:46.4180319Z 
2026-11-06T02:58:46.4180439Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T02:58:46.4180574Z 
2026-11-06T02:58:46.4180704Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T02:58:46.4180952Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T02:58:46.4181078Z 
2026-11-06T02:58:46.4181148Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T02:58:46.4181342Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T02:58:46.4181546Z 
2026-11-06T02:58:46.4181731Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T02:58:46.4181962Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T02:58:46.4182053Z 
